 box cricket court construction take? <span style="color:#c0392b;font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:300;">+</span></summary><p style="color:#4b5563;line-height:1.7;padding-bottom:1rem;">A standard 60ft x 100ft box cricket court takes 15-20 working days from bare ground or RCC slab to playing-ready handover.</p></details><details class="faq-item" style="border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 0;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a2e;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">Can box cricket be built on a rooftop? <span style="color:#c0392b;font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:300;">+</span></summary><p style="color:#4b5563;line-height:1.7;padding-bottom:1rem;">Yes. NettingTeam has completed 50+ rooftop box cricket setups in Hyderabad. We coordinate with structural engineers for load capacity assessment before every rooftop project.</p></details><details class="faq-item" style="border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 0;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a2e;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">What net material is used for box cricket cage? <span style="color:#c0392b;font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:300;">+</span></summary><p style="color:#4b5563;line-height:1.7;padding-bottom:1rem;">UV-stabilized HDPE or knotted nylon nets with 40mm-50mm square mesh and 1.5mm-2.5mm yarn thickness. GI wire rope tensioning keeps all panels drum-tight for safe ball containment.</p></details>  </div>
